  "qualification": "Five Linux network tests passed under original net/mount/PID wrapper; original loadgen fails three delayed cohort cases. Separate 6/150-client DHCP functional receipt is required alongside. No performance acceptance claim.",
  "limitations": [
    "Only fixed-rate no-saturation DNS and DHCP renew-only are changed; closed-loop, explicit saturation and full DHCP-cycle workload retain old paths.",
    "Pending work is represented by three u64 values per client, with one outstanding I/O per client; original planned sequence/phase/due timestamps remain authoritative.",
    "The cutoff is admission of queued work until measurement_end + timeout_ms, not a new wire-send deadline. Existing TCP connection timeout and response deadlines remain; deferred sends and late completions remain visible in lag/latency records.",
    "Unadmitted work at cutoff remains explicitly skipped; response timeout/wrong/transport errors are not converted into passes.",
    "The first macOS test setup could not compile the existing Linux-only upstream (ppoll); no tests ran there. Native loadgen strict compilation passed. A preliminary Linux-host-loopback run is retained separately; the final evidence here uses the original isolated wrapper."
  ],
